# Cloudflare-first

- Check current Cloudflare documentation before changing bindings, Wrangler config, or runtime APIs.
- Evaluate a native Cloudflare capability first, but document and use a non-Cloudflare option when
  requirements, reliability, portability, compliance, or cost evidence makes it better.
- Keep `wrangler.jsonc`, generated binding types, migrations, tests, and runtime usage aligned.
- Never add real account IDs, resource IDs, domains, sender identities, secrets, OTPs, or user data.
- Treat https://congtam.net/brandguide as the brand source of truth; do not duplicate its content.
- Add only services the app needs. Treat rate limits as abuse friction, not exact accounting.
- Log privacy-safe event metadata and request IDs, never payloads, credentials, or identity data.
- Changes learned from this app do not silently sync to the template. Submit an evidence-backed
  proposal with reproduction, current docs, tests, migration guidance, and human review.
